1","UniEvo-VL: An On-policy Self-Distillation Training Recipe for Multimodal Model Self-improvement",142,"2026-10-01"],["2608.16590","Zetta ζ: An Efficient Closed-Loop Embodied Harness for Self-Evolving Physical Intelligence",141,"2026-08-20"],["2608.09819","Macaron-V1: Towards Open Continual Learning with Self-Improvement and Mixture-of-LoRA",113,"2026-08-11"],["2609.15779","EvoOntology: A Self-Evolving Ontology Layer for Data Agents",104,"2026-09-21"],["2609.38288","AREX-2: Advancing Self-Improving Agents through Long-Horizon Reflective Tasks",93,"2026-10-01"]],"featured":[{"id":"2611.06910","date":"2026-11-05","title":"FrontierPhysics: Evaluating Agents for End-to-End Physics Research","tldr":"FrontierPhysics has 42 physicists turn their own research into 56 end-to-end tasks, and no AI agent configuration passes more than 46 of 168 attempts."},{"id":"2610.41956","date":"2026-11-02","title":"Chronos-2: A foundation model for multivariate time series forecasting","tldr":"Chronos-2 is a 120M-parameter zero-shot forecaster that uses group attention to learn relationships among related series and covariates in context, trained only on synthetic multivariate data."},{"id":"2610.33624","date":"2026-10-29","title":"RSI Arena: Towards Recursive Self-Improvement with Human Feedback","tldr":"Ten frontier models were each given six days to autonomously post-train the same 30B base model; the best, trained by GPT-6 Astra, tied NVIDIA's own instruct model in style-controlled human ratings."},{"id":"2610.35962","date":"2026-10-28","title":"h1: A Taste of the Bitter Lesson in Automated Theorem Proving","tldr":"A bare-bones agent loop around the Lean proof checker, given enough budget, matches or beats elaborate theorem-proving pipelines at the same model and settles eight open Formal Conjectures problems."},{"id":"2610.33845","date":"2026-10-27","title":"Build, Don't Play: Self-Improving LLM Research Agents Develop a Hearthstone Battlegrounds AI That Rivals Top Players","tldr":"LLM research agents built a faithful Hearthstone Battlegrounds simulator and an RL agent in 20 days; the agent outperformed the server's top-10 players' recent results, while frontier LLMs playing directly fell far short."},{"id":"2610.32770","date":"2026-10-26","title":"On-Policy Self-Training: Data-Free Self-Improvement in Large Language Models","tldr":"Given only topic names, a model writes its own problems and answer hints, then distills from a copy of itself that sees the hints, improving MMLU by 10 points with no curated prompts or answers."},{"id":"2610.28594","date":"2026-10-24","title":"Learning the 4D World through Point Trajectory Forecasting","tldr":"Training a multi-view video world model to also forecast where tracked 3D points will move yields more faithful futures than a video-only twin and higher robot success rates."},{"id":"2610.24944","date":"2026-10-22","title":"Epi: Towards a Persistent, Self-Improving Agent for Autonomous Research","tldr":"Épi, a persistent research agent with memory, branching and independent review, sets 120 verified records on math constants and constructions and a computer-assisted case of Tuza's conjecture, and its Épi-turbo variant beats Codex on cost."},{"id":"2610.22791","date":"2026-10-20","title":"Self-Evolving Coding Agents via Harness-Policy Optimization","tldr":"Self-HPO alternates between letting a coding agent rewrite its own harness and training it with reinforcement learning, lifting Qwen3.5-35B-A3B's average resolve rate across three SWE-Bench variants from 57.8% to 64.8%."},{"id":"2610.13917","date":"2026-10-12","title":"Designing Protein Structures from Natural Language","tldr":"Prompteina generates all-atom protein structures and sequences from plain-language prompts, trained on 52 million captions, and produced nine lab-confirmed binders against a target that had no reported de novo binders."},{"id":"2610.08902","date":"2026-10-09","title":"Agent Plasticity: Measuring Self-Improvement Through Experience","tldr":"Agent Plasticity measures how efficiently a frozen-weight agent turns experience into held-out gains, showing that the model with the best final score is not the one that improves most efficiently."},{"id":"2610.11959","date":"2026-10-09","title":"MiMo-V2.6: Scaling Reinforcement Learning Towards Self-Improvement","tldr":"Xiaomi's MiMo-V2.6 report details a 1.02T-parameter MoE trained with heavily scaled agentic RL, including costs, environments, grading and reward-hacking defenses, and releases its training dynamics, environments and RL framework."}]}